    "result_text": "All tests pass with a clean build. Here's what I implemented for the telephone-normalization rule on `POST /api/owners`:\n\n**Change to the create pipeline** \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields.java` (the first step):\n- After the existing missing/blank checks, it strips every non-digit character from `telephone` (`replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`).\n- If the stripped value is not exactly 10 digits, it throws a new checked `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 400.\n- Otherwise it writes the normalized 10-digit value back onto the DTO (`request.setTelephone(...)`) before republishing, so `BuildOwner` \u2192 `SaveOwner` store it and `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/GET return it.\n\n**New escalation** (following the repo's error convention, not `@ControllerAdvice`):\n- `InvalidTelephoneException` (extends `Exception`, so it's on the `throws` clause).\n- `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"telephone\"]}`, matching the existing `MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` style.\n- `officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.InvalidTelephoneException.yml` wiring the handler.\n\n**Test results:**\n- `coreStripsToTenDigits`: `\"(04) 1234-5678\"` \u2192 stored/returned as `\"0412345678\"` \u2705\n- `errorRejectsTooFewDigits`: `\"12345\"` \u2192 400 \u2705\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nOrdering note: the blank/missing check runs first (a null/blank telephone stays a `MissingOwnerFieldsException`), and normalization+length happens only for a present value \u2014 so a non-digit-only value like `\"abc\"` strips to empty and is correctly rejected as not-10-digits.",
